---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import OperatorContact from '../components/OperatorContact.astro';
import { operator } from '../data/policies';
const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['scope', 'Scope'],
  ['eligibility', 'Refund eligibility'],
  ['request', 'Requesting help'],
  ['cancel', 'Cancelling a subscription'],
  ['credits', 'Credits and refunded access'],
  ['changes', 'Policy changes'],
];
---

<Policy
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How purchase refunds, subscription cancellation and credit adjustments will be handled."
  path="/refund"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>1. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      Paid PaperEnjoyer plans and credit packs are coming soon. This policy describes future
      purchases completed through Paddle. It does not create a purchase or charge for downloading
      the current free app.
    </p>
    <p>
      Paddle will be the merchant of record. Its{' '}
      <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/buyer-terms">Buyer Terms</a> govern transaction refunds,
      subject to your mandatory rights. PaperEnjoyer offers no additional unconditional money-back
      guarantee.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="eligibility">
    <h2>2. Refund eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      Refunds depend on applicable law and Paddle’s policy. A discretionary request within 14 days
      is not a guaranteed refund. Regional withdrawal rights and remedies for defective or
      misdescribed products remain available. See Paddle’s policy for the rules and deadlines
      applicable to your location and transaction.
    </p>
    <p>
      Using an AI feature does not, by itself, establish a valid waiver of statutory rights. Any
      exception depends on the legal requirements, including consent where required.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="request">
    <h2>3. Requesting help</h2>
    <p>
      For a Paddle order, use <a href="https://paddle.net/">Paddle’s buyer support</a> or the
      support link in your receipt. Paddle handles the payment refund. You can also email us for
      help identifying an order or resolving a product problem.
    </p>
    <p>
      Include the purchasing email, order reference if available, purchase date and a brief
      description of the issue. For a technical problem, an app version and a redacted screenshot
      can help. Do not send passwords, API keys, complete card numbers or confidential papers.
    </p>
    <p>
      For missing entitlements, duplicate charges or a failed task, contact{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a>. A support investigation does not
      require you to give up a legal remedy or let a statutory deadline expire.
    </p>
    <OperatorContact />
  </section>
  <section id="cancel">
    <h2>4. Cancelling a subscription</h2>
    <p>
      When subscriptions launch, use the management link in your Paddle receipt or contact Paddle to
      cancel before renewal. Your paid benefits continue through the current period; cancellation
      stops future renewals. Cancellation and a refund request are different actions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Uninstalling PaperEnjoyer does not cancel billing. Contact us if you cannot locate your
      receipt or need assistance.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="credits">
    <h2>5. Credits and refunded access</h2>
    <p>
      Credits measure use of PaperEnjoyer’s software. The planned registration gift has no purchase
      price to refund. Purchased packs do not expire through monthly resets or ordinary subscription
      cancellation, but they remain subject to any refund or reversal of their purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      A correction to an incorrectly charged task allowance is an account credit adjustment,
      separate from a payment refund. We will investigate usage discrepancies rather than promise
      that every unsuccessful task qualifies for the same remedy.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a purchase is refunded, access or credits attributable to that purchase may be withdrawn. A
      cash-redemption restriction does not override an applicable purchase-refund right.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="changes">
    <h2>6. Policy changes</h2>
    <p>
      We will date future changes on this page. Changes do not retroactively reduce rights attached
      to an earlier transaction. Keep your receipt and the purchase terms for reference.
    </p>
  </section>
</Policy>
